  "description": "A charming red brick period residence in the heart of Dublin 8, boasting elegant original features, two spacious bedrooms and a private rear garden with valuable rear lane access.\n\nA beautifully presented red brick terraced residence of immense character and charm, ideally situated in the heart of Dublin 8, showcasing elegant period features and generous living accommodation throughout.\n\nSavills are delighted to present 7 Greenville Avenue, a most attractive two-bedroom terraced home that seamlessly combines timeless classical design with modern living. Behind its handsome red brick façade lies a welcoming and well-appointed interior, featuring an abundance of original-style detailing including ornate ceiling coving, decorative ceiling roses and feature fireplaces that enhance the property's period appeal.\n\nThe accommodation extends to a bright entrance hallway which leads to an elegant living room, complete with a feature fireplace and beautiful ornate coving. Interconnecting into the dining room, creating an ideal space for both everyday living and entertaining. The dining room also benefits from a beautiful fireplace and flows seamlessly through to the fully fitted kitchen. Finished with integrated appliances, a solid wood counter, a traditional Belfast sink and tiled flooring, the kitchen offers both style and practicality.\n\nTo the rear, a private low-maintenance garden has been thoughtfully designed with timber panelling and a granite slab patio, providing a wonderful outdoor entertaining space. A particularly valuable feature is the rear pedestrian access onto a laneway behind the property.\n\nUpstairs, there are two spacious double bedrooms, both retaining attractive cast iron fireplaces that further reflect the home's character. One of the bedrooms also benefits from fitted wardrobes, providing excellent storage. The family bathroom is fully tiled and is fitted with a bath incorporating an electric shower overhead.\n\n7 Greenville Avenue presents a rare opportunity to acquire a charming period home in one of Dublin 8's most sought-after residential locations. With its wealth of original features, practical layout and attractive rear garden with rear access, this exceptional property is sure to appeal to a wide range of purchasers seeking a home of distinction within easy reach of the city centre.\n\nSet in one of Dublin 8's most sought-after residential enclaves, 7 Greenville Avenue is conveniently located just a short walk from Portobello, Camden Street and St Stephen's Green. The property is ideally positioned to take advantage of Dublin's finest shopping, business and entertainment destinations. A wide selection of cafés, restaurants and artisan shops are located within walking distance including the highly regarded Marlowe & Co and The Fumbally, two of the neighbourhood's most popular cafes. Camden Street and Portobello provide further choice, with some of the city's best known restaurants and social destinations just minutes away. Everyday conveniences are all within walking distance.\n\nThe location offers excellent access to major institutions, with Trinity College Dublin and St James's Hospital a short commute, making the area particularly attractive for those working or studying in the city centre. Residents enjoy close proximity to Iveagh Gardens, St Stephen's Green and the scenic Grand Canal walkways, offering attractive green spaces for relaxation, exercise and outdoor leisure. \n\nThe area is exceptionally well served by public transport, with numerous bus routes along Clanbrassil Street and South Circular Road while the Luas Green Line at Harcourt provides swift access across the city. Perfectly positioned in the heart of Dublin 8, 7 Greenville Avenue provides an unrivalled blend of convenience, accessibility and urban living.",
